Day 40: Behold Your King | Palm Sunday (Holy Week Begins)

📌 YouTube Description
“Hosanna to the Son of David!”
A humble King.
A gentle Savior.
A love that rides straight into the heart of the Passion.

Welcome to Day 40 of our Lent journey, the doorway into Holy Week.
Today’s reflection invites you to behold Jesus as He enters Jerusalem — not with force or spectacle, but with humility, courage, and self‑giving love. Palm Sunday is a paradox: a celebration wrapped in sorrow, a triumph that leads to a cross, a King who conquers not by taking life but by giving His own.

This spoken‑word devotional draws you into the mystery of a Savior who knows what awaits Him — betrayal, suffering, the weight of the world’s sin — and still chooses love. He is the King who does not rule by fear, but by compassion. The King who does not demand perfection, but invites your heart.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Palm Sunday begins the great mystery of Holy Week

How Jesus enters Jerusalem as a humble, self‑giving King

Why His love is revealed most fully in the Passion

A prayer to enter Holy Week with reverence and openness

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, I welcome You.”

